WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.100
In HeLa cells, the inside of a mitochondrion measured close to pH 8.

2
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.760
The Golgi measured close to pH 6.6.

3
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.580
In mammalian cells, the lysosome sits at pH 4.5 to 5.

4
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.520
All three share one cytosol.

5
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.200
So how does one cell keep them apart?

6
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:30.483
pH is a logarithm, so a small gap hides a large difference.

7
00:00:31.443 --> 00:00:32.923
Take the two HeLa averages.

8
00:00:33.703 --> 00:00:36.023
The Golgi reads 6.58.

9
00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:40.363
The mitochondrial matrix is estimated at 7.98.

10
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:43.103
They differ by 1.4.

11
00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:47.103
10 to the power 1.4 is about 25.

12
00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:52.763
So the Golgi has about 25 times the free proton activity of the matrix.

13
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.343
Think of a room with its own thermostat.

14
00:00:56.963 --> 00:00:58.983
The wall does not make the room warm.

15
00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:03.423
It slows the loss of heat, so a heater can hold the set point.

16
00:01:04.423 --> 00:01:06.083
A cell works the same way.

17
00:01:06.803 --> 00:01:08.083
The pump is the heater.

18
00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:10.143
Leak is the lost heat.

19
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.263
Every difference is a steady state.

20
00:01:13.863 --> 00:01:17.823
It lasts only while the pump keeps paying, usually in ATP.

21
00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:21.263
Stop the pump, and the difference runs down.

22
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:26.167
For protons, the pump is the V-ATPase.

23
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:31.747
It spends ATP to move protons from the cytosol into a lumen.

24
00:01:32.687 --> 00:01:36.567
In HeLa cells, a drug called bafilomycin blocks it.

25
00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:39.427
Then the Golgi became less acid.

26
00:01:40.227 --> 00:01:43.027
So the acidity of the Golgi is not simply there.

27
00:01:43.027 --> 00:01:44.767
It is actively kept.

28
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.990
Calcium follows the same rule.

29
00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:53.470
The pump SERCA moves calcium from the cytosol into the ER.

30
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.950
The ER lumen holds about half to one millimolar free calcium.

31
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.810
The cytosol holds about 100 nanomolar.

32
00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:07.370
That is a 5,000- to 10,000-fold difference.

33
00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:13.190
Block SERCA with thapsigargin, and calcium leaks out faster than it is replaced.

34
00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.723
Not every compartment is acid.

35
00:02:17.423 --> 00:02:22.183
The ER is near neutral, and the mitochondrial matrix is alkaline.

36
00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:25.603
Each lumen settles at its own value.

37
00:02:26.263 --> 00:02:29.803
That value is a steady state between pumping and leak.

38
00:02:30.543 --> 00:02:31.743
It is not set once.

39
00:02:32.623 --> 00:02:36.143
A luminal difference lasts only while a pump keeps paying.
